			<div class="content" id="post-content-2169382">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Headcanon,&nbsp;activate!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;IT&nbsp;WAS&nbsp;ALL&nbsp;A&nbsp;DREAM&nbsp;OK&nbsp;NOT&nbsp;REALLY</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>My concept on this is that the four who attempted to gain access to the house are members of the GOI, which is also responsible for the phenomenon. The phenomenon is difficult to achieve but replicable and the group as a whole will eventually move on to focusing on their next location but, at the least, would like to deactivate 2377 so that outsiders don't have access.</p>
<p>2377 is their church, in a manner of speaking. The act of murder, specifically in these cases of the victim's isolation, is important to them. I don't want to go over all the whats and whys yet as I intend to eventually have more skips and tales with the GOI becoming more fully understood.</p>
<p>A rewrite consideration I've had is having the incident log extend to several break-in attempts of increasing size, but I've not decided if I want to do that yet or to what degree. It may help relay the importance of 2377 to the GOI though.</p>
</div>
